### Compute Separation — E2E HTTP Testing
###
### These requests exercise the compute separation admin APIs end-to-end.
### Run them top-to-bottom to simulate the full platform orchestration flow.
###
### Prerequisites:
###   1. Start the Aspire harness: dotnet run --project tools/ComputeSeparation/AppHost
###      (use --UseContainers true for container mode)
###   2. Wait for all resources to show as Running in the Aspire dashboard.
###
### The encrypted payloads use the well-known CONTAINER_ENCRYPTION_KEY from the
### Aspire harness: 0F75CA46E7EBDD39E4CA6B074D1F9A5972B849A55F91A248F6B038A61BACE9D7

@runtimeHost = http://localhost:7071
@workerProxyHost = http://localhost:50054
@masterKey = dev-master-key

### ============================================================
### Full Orchestration Flow
### ============================================================
###
### This mirrors what the platform (RCP → NNA) does in production:
###
###   1. Wait for worker proxy readiness (/admin/worker/ready on worker proxy)
###   2. Specialize the worker (/admin/worker/assign on worker proxy)
###      → Proxy drives: WorkerInit → EnvReload → MetadataPrefetch
###      → Proxy caches all responses for later replay
###   3. Specialize the runtime (/admin/instance/assign on runtime)
###      → Runtime exits placeholder mode, applies app settings
###   4. Link the worker to the runtime (/admin/workers/link on runtime)
###      → Runtime connects to proxy gRPC, receives cached init + metadata
###      → ScriptHost starts, functions loaded, host becomes Running
###   5. Invoke a function (GET /api/HttpTrigger)
###      → Runtime → Proxy (gRPC invocation + HTTP forward) → Worker
###
### ============================================================

### Step 1: Check worker proxy readiness
### NNA polls this until the worker has connected to the proxy via gRPC.
GET {{workerProxyHost}}/admin/worker/ready

###

### Step 2: Specialize the worker
### NNA calls this after /admin/worker/ready succeeds. The proxy drives the full
### init + specialization + metadata prefetch sequence with the worker,
### caching all responses for later replay to the runtime.
POST {{workerProxyHost}}/admin/worker/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "environment": {
    "FUNCTIONS_WORKER_RUNTIME": "dotnet-isolated",
    "WEBSITE_SITE_NAME": "devhost"
  },
  "functionAppDirectory": "/home/site/wwwroot"
}

###

### Step 3: Specialize the runtime (simulate platform /assign call)
### NNA calls this to take the runtime out of placeholder mode.
### The payload is AES-256-CBC encrypted with CONTAINER_ENCRYPTION_KEY.
### Plaintext: {"SiteId":1234,"SiteName":"devhost","Environment":{"FUNCTIONS_WORKER_EXTERNAL_ENABLED":"true","FUNCTIONS_WORKER_RUNTIME":"dotnet-isolated","WEBSITE_SITE_NAME":"devhost"}}
POST {{runtimeHost}}/admin/instance/assign?code={{masterKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedContext": "5HK2jK+MejSDtjZXWzDIMA==.gGbJ+jcHOTTTOfMY81WR+b51MrKffae+WonFrjoYdQC5GS5hqRW0Bvgvmbze5Y6SgWxTD30vvZnv3lKYWKB0KotvpgjyxMBCyYtbQYKdCM7sScZlvh0vgSOzgxJO6xqJySzW7w/gWYXAKnJvYBUrMFzw9656+YwEQ8osVPsuJGld9Fy2lND3nwgKvbxpcZde/3k2mt0OWOPHvKgHi9Z6duS7OFYeFuRbFHbJ0I/GVrg=.l7sP0SVC5PPsmjsAf9df4iUs609Ck09VtyO6LEvhMVs="
}

###

### Step 4: Link the worker to the runtime
### RCP calls this after both sides are specialized. The runtime establishes
### an outbound gRPC connection to the worker proxy. The proxy replays cached
### StartStream, WorkerInitResponse (with host.json + capabilities), and
### FunctionMetadataResponse. This triggers ScriptHost startup and function loading.
POST {{runtimeHost}}/admin/workers/link?code={{masterKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workerId": "w_test01",
  "podName": "worker-pod-test01",
  "grpcEndpoint": "{{workerGrpcEndpoint}}",
  "podKey": "test-key"
}

###

### Step 5: Invoke a function (after host reaches Running state)
### The runtime routes the HTTP request through the proxy to the worker.
### gRPC InvocationRequest flows runtime → proxy → worker.
### HTTP request flows runtime → proxy HTTP port → worker HTTP listener.
GET {{runtimeHost}}/api/HttpTrigger

###

### ============================================================
### Diagnostics & Monitoring
### ============================================================

### Get host status (check state, function count, worker count)
GET {{runtimeHost}}/admin/host/status?code={{masterKey}}

###

### Ping the host (lightweight health check)
GET {{runtimeHost}}/admin/host/ping

###

### Poll worker instance state (long-polling)
### Send with revision 0 to get current state immediately.
### Send with the last known revision to block until state changes.
### Response follows the FunctionsWorkerPod schema:
###   { functionsContainerType, podName, revision, state: { podStatus, runtimePodName, ... } }
POST {{workerProxyHost}}/admin/infra/instanceState
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "revision": 0
}

###

### ============================================================
### Lifecycle Management
### ============================================================

### Trigger worker drain (scale-in scenario)
### Worker proxy accepts the drain reason, maps it to a replacement policy,
### transitions to Draining, and sends WorkerDrainRequest to runtime over gRPC.
### Runtime drains in-flight invocations and sends WorkerDrainComplete back.
POST {{workerProxyHost}}/admin/worker/drain
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "IdleScaleIn"
}

###

### Stop the runtime instance (full runtime stop)
### Drains host listeners, disconnects all workers, sends WorkerDrainComplete to each.
POST {{runtimeHost}}/admin/instance/stop?code={{masterKey}}
